This project is a website for the Roblox game "Divine Rarities".
The website is projected to have 3 main parts: the wiki, calculators, and guides.

- Wiki: the first point of interest. Human-readable rendering of `src/data/runes.json` (converted from the dev's `message.txt`), plus other game info (worlds, codes, stats, etc.) as it becomes available.
- Calculators: tools based on the roll model, e.g. "I have 100k RPS, how long to get 10 copies of this secret rune?".
- Guides: written guides to help new players (order of things to do, hints for secret codes, etc.).

The website is hosted on GitHub Pages (auto-deploy via GitHub Actions workflow in `.github/workflows/`). In dev it runs on Vite (`npm run dev`).

All code is JavaScript, no TypeScript.

Stack / layout:
- Vanilla JS + Vite (no framework). Tabs are switched client-side via hash routes (`#/wiki`, `#/calculators`, `#/guides`).
- Rune data lives in `src/data/runes.json` (checked in), generated by `scripts/convert-runes.mjs` from the raw luau source `message.txt` at the project root.
- The website's structure is:
  [Name, eventually logo of website] [version]   <- version = site version, read from package.json
  [Tabs]
  L> Wiki, Calculators, Guides
  [Footer]

